# Exclude build artifacts and large directories from Docker build context
# to prevent slow COPY operations and oversized build contexts.

# Rust build targets (everywhere in the repo)
**/target/

# Node.js
**/node_modules/

# Swift / SwiftPM — NOT needed by any Rust image build.
# `.build/` is SwiftPM's dependency + artifact cache and is the single largest
# thing in this repo outside target/ (~7 GB: firebase-ios-sdk git packs, gRPC
# xcframeworks, snowplow checkouts). Without this exclusion every `*-image`
# build copies it into the build context — tens of GB of pointless I/O per
# build, which is what tipped this machine into memory-compressor/swap
# exhaustion and a watchdog panic (2026-09-23). The whole app dir goes, not
# just `.build/`, so Xcode state can never leak back in.
**/.build/
**/DerivedData/
apps/yral-ios/

# Git
.git/
.gitignore

# Python
.venv/
*.pyc

# Ansible (not needed for builds)
ansible/

# Kubernetes manifests (not needed for builds)
kubernetes/

# Dockerfiles themselves (copied individually by BuildKit)
# (Don't ignore them — Shipwright needs to read them)

# IDE / editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Misc
*.md
TODO.md
LICENSE
mise.lock
spacetime*.json